menu "EGOS SDK"

    config EGOS_ETHERNET_ENABLED
        bool "Enable W5500 Ethernet support"
        default n
        select ETH_USE_SPI_ETHERNET
        select ETH_SPI_ETHERNET_W5500
        help
            Enable W5500 SPI Ethernet as a network option.
            When enabled, the connection manager tries Ethernet first
            before falling back to WiFi.

            This pulls in the ESP-IDF W5500 SPI driver it depends on, so
            enabling this option is sufficient on its own. Without those
            selects, egos_ethernet.c fails to compile with implicit
            declarations of esp_eth_mac_new_w5500 and esp_eth_phy_new_w5500,
            and every consumer has to know to set them by hand.

    config EGOS_STATUS_LED_ENABLED
        bool "Enable RGB status LED"
        default n
        help
            Enable RGB LED status indicator via LEDC PWM.
            Shows connection state through color patterns.

endmenu
